{"base_rate":0.5761154855643045,"brier":0.229940157480315,"bss":0.05841891718442549,"bss_hi":0.19754754639012925,"bss_lo":-0.0853170945724705,"chart":{"base":[809.0,213.2],"fp":[582.2,383.7],"lead":"62,260.7 272,234.3 482,200 692,134.1","note":{"base":"skill 0.06 — higher than 9% of cities","fp":"low end +31pp, high end -2pp","lead":"day-1 error 1.0 °C — better than 69% of cities","rel":"promised 0% → rained 24%; promised 97% → rained 95%"},"rel":"62,363.9 134.1,228.2 482.7,108.5 676.2,55.1"},"country":"FR","deep":false,"depth":["Rain-probability calibration","Calibration curve","Seasonal split"],"ece":0.22270341207349076,"ess":376.6959043016697,"html":{"answer":"\n<h2 id=\"answer\">The short answer for Nantes</h2>\n<div class=\"verdict\">\n<p class=\"lead\"><b>The Nantes rain forecast is only marginally better than quoting the long-run average, though 4 points on its probability scale are off by more than chance explains.</b></p>\n<p>When it says rain is <i>near certain</i> (97%), believe about\n<b>95%</b>. When it says rain is <i>very unlikely</i>\n(0%), there is still roughly a <b>24%</b> chance.</p>\n<p class=\"muted\">Based on 762 days, 2024-04-26 to\n2026-05-31. \"Rain\" means at least 0.2 mm measured at\nNANTES-BOUGUENAIS, 8.5 km from the forecast grid point.\nSkill score 0.06, ranked 122 of\n134 &mdash; but see the rank <i>range</i>\n(104&ndash;129) before reading anything into\nthat position.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h3>What the percentages actually mean here</h3>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th class=\"num\">It said</th><th class=\"num\">It rained</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Days</th><th>Verdict</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class='num'>0%</td><td class='num'><b>24%</b></td><td class='num'>275</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>4%</td><td class='num'><b>49%</b></td><td class='num'>98</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>20%</td><td class='num'><b>62%</b></td><td class='num'>80</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>54%</td><td class='num'><b>80%</b></td><td class='num'>79</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>82%</td><td class='num'><b>86%</b></td><td class='num'>66</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>97%</td><td class='num'><b>95%</b></td><td class='num'>164</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">4 of 6 groups are further from honest than chance\nalone can explain. The rest are indistinguishable from a perfect forecast.</p>\n","card":"\n<div class=\"gcard\">\n  <p class=\"gcard-head\"><b>Nantes</b> <span class=\"muted\">FR</span></p>\n  <p class=\"gcard-tier\"><span class=\"tag bad\">Barely beats the average</span>\n    <span class=\"muted\">4 points off by more than chance</span></p>\n  <dl class=\"gcard-stats\">\n    <div><dt>Skill score</dt><dd>0.06</dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Rank</dt><dd>104&ndash;129\n      <span class=\"muted\">of 134</span></dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Record</dt><dd>762 <span class=\"muted\">days</span></dd></div>\n  </dl>\n  <p class=\"gcard-more\"><a href=\"#answer\">The full verdict for\n    Nantes &darr;</a></p>\n</div>","curve":"\n<h2 id=\"curve\">The calibration curve</h2>\n<p>Each dot is a group of days sharing a similar forecast. Horizontal position\nis what was promised; vertical is what happened. <b>On the dashed diagonal =\nhonest.</b> Hover any dot for its sample size.</p>\n<figure><svg viewBox=\"0 0 430 430\" width=\"100%\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Calibration curve for Nantes\"><rect class=\"chart-plot\" x=\"58\" y=\"18\" width=\"354\" height=\"364\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"58\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"382\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"58\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">0%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"386\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">0%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"146.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"146.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"291.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"291.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"146.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">25%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"295.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">25%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"235.0\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"235.0\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"200.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"200.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">50%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"204.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">50%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"323.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"323.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"109.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"109.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"323.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">75%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"113.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">75%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"412\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"18\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"412\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">100%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"22\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">100%</text><polygon class=\"chart-band\" points=\"58.0,382.0 73.46040816326531,348.57142857142856 129.2425,272.8 248.89113924050636,147.0126582278481 348.8163636363636,51.09090909090912 403.15,20.21951219512198 403.15,35.756097560975604 348.8163636363636,117.27272727272725 248.89113924050636,225.34177215189874 129.2425,336.61375 73.46040816326531,378.2857142857143 58.0,382.0\" opacity=\"0.16\"/><line class=\"chart-ideal\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\" stroke-dasharray=\"5,4\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"/><line class=\"chart-base\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"172.29396325459317\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"172.29396325459317\" stroke-dasharray=\"2,3\"/><polyline class=\"chart-line\" points=\"58.0,295.9636363636364 73.46040816326531,203.71428571428572 129.2425,154.5 248.89113924050636,91.72151898734177 348.8163636363636,67.63636363636363 403.15,35.756097560975604\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2.4\"/><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 0%&amp;#10;It rained 24% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 275 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"58.0\" cy=\"295.9636363636364\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 4%&amp;#10;It rained 49% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 98 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"73.46040816326531\" cy=\"203.71428571428572\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 20%&amp;#10;It rained 62% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 80 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"129.2425\" cy=\"154.5\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 54%&amp;#10;It rained 80% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 79 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"248.89113924050636\" cy=\"91.72151898734177\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 82%&amp;#10;It rained 86% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 66 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"348.8163636363636\" cy=\"67.63636363636363\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 97%&amp;#10;It rained 95% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 164 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"403.15\" cy=\"35.756097560975604\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"422\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\">What the forecast promised</text><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"15\" y=\"200.0\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" transform=\"rotate(-90 15 200.0)\">How often it actually rained</text></svg>\n<figcaption>Green band = where a <b>flawless</b> forecast would still land, given\nhow few days we have. Red dots fall outside it, so those are real errors rather\nthan noise. The faint horizontal line is climatology\n(58%).</figcaption></figure>\n","season":"\n<h2 id=\"season\">Does the season matter?</h2>\n<p>In Nantes the forecast is most skilful in\n<b>spring</b> (0.20) and least in\n<b>winter</b> (-0.09).</p>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th>Season</th><th class=\"num\">Days</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Rain days</th><th class=\"num\">Skill score</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Avg error</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>winter</td><td class='num'>180</td><td class='num'>69%</td><td class='num'>-0.093</td><td class='num'>19.9%</td></tr><tr><td>autumn</td><td class='num'>180</td><td class='num'>62%</td><td class='num'>-0.052</td><td class='num'>23.4%</td></tr><tr><td>summer</td><td class='num'>184</td><td class='num'>48%</td><td class='num'>0.019</td><td class='num'>24.3%</td></tr><tr><td>spring</td><td class='num'>218</td><td class='num'>53%</td><td class='num'>0.204</td><td class='num'>19.6%</td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">Four-way splits of a two-year record are thin, so read the\nordering as indicative. Coarser binning is used here than for the annual curve\nfor the same reason.</p>\n"},"lat":47.21725,"lon":-1.55336,"n":762,"n_cities":134,"name":"Nantes","offset_days":0,"pop_map":[{"hi":0.03,"lo":0.0,"mean":0.0,"n":275,"obs":0.23636363636363636,"sig":true},{"hi":0.1,"lo":0.03,"mean":0.043673469387755105,"n":98,"obs":0.4897959183673469,"sig":true},{"hi":0.35,"lo":0.1,"mean":0.20125,"n":80,"obs":0.625,"sig":true},{"hi":0.75,"lo":0.35,"mean":0.539240506329114,"n":79,"obs":0.797